{title: 523 - My Faith Has Found a Resting Place}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #523 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 523}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]My faith has found a resting place,
[G]Not in [C/G]a [C#m/G#]manmade [Am]creed;
[Em/B]I trust the [D/A]Everliving [Em/B]One,
[G]That He for me will plead.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]I need no [C/G]other [C#m/G#]evidence,
[Em/B]I need [D/A]no other [Em/B]plea;
[Bm]It is enough [G]that Jesus died,
[C/G]And rose [D7/C]again [Em/B]for [D/A]me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Enough for me that Jesus saves,
[G]This ends [C/G]my [C#m/G#]fear [Am]and doubt;
[Em/B]A sinful [D/A]soul, I come [Em/B]to Him,
[G]He will not cast me out.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]My soul is resting on the Word,
[G]The living [C#m/G#]Word [Am]of God,
[Em/B]Salvation [D/A]in my Savior's [Em/B]name,
[G]Salvation through His blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]My great Physician heals the sick,
[G]The lost [C/G]He [C#m/G#]came [Am]to save;
[Em/B]For me His [D/A]precious blood [Em/B]He shed,
[G]For me His life He gave.
{end_of_verse}
